    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/026-publish-size.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an identified document filed to a matter, when the Save tab renders, then a card shows record type, name, and number for that matter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the implementation, when reviewed, then `notes/026-slot-scope-decision.md` and the PR description both enumerate all candidate association slots, name the subset the card reads, and give a reason for each exclusion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a document with more than one association slot populated, when the card renders, then it applies the documented precedence rule deterministically — the same input always yields the same card.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the card, when it renders, then it is a separate component from `RelatedToPicker.tsx` and the picker's behavior is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an identified document with no populated association in the read scope, when the Save tab renders, then an explicit no-association state appears — not an empty card, not a blank region, not an error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a caller without read access to the related record, when the read surface is invoked, then the record's name and number are NOT returned and the response is a ProblemDetails 403 or an empty association — asserted by a contract test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given no resolved document identity, when the Save tab renders, then the card is absent and no association read call is made.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every association GUID is canonicalized via `cleanGuid` at every boundary and never appears raw in an OData key predicate; verified by inspection during code review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Office theme set to Dark, when the card renders in any state, then every color resolves from a Fluent v9 semantic token and no hex literal appears in the added styles.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git diff --name-only` shows no change to files `unified-access-control-r2` task 095 is modifying; `/conflict-check` was run before the PR and its result is cited.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run typecheck` is clean for the files this task touched; `npm test` and `npm run build` pass; `dotnet build` and the Office contract tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size is measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with `Compress-Archive`, both absolute sizes and the delta are recorded, and the delta is under the +5 MB escalation threshold.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-09 and its cross-project coordination row; plan.md §2 (Dataverse schema validated live — the two-slot model is already in schema, no schema task needed) and §4 Phase 2 task 026. The direct-versus-related asymmetry is real and load-bearing: the Office save path writes only the direct slots, so a card that reads only `sprk_related*` would be empty on every document the add-in itself created.
  </notes>

